description "AppArmor: the parser, the profile store and aa-status, which a deb-family container image carries none of"

supports "debian" "ubuntu"

provides "apparmor-policy"

requires "build-environment"

// The capability is declared by whoever carries the parser, base or module —
// the rule `graph.rs` implements and the one SELinux has always followed.
// `ghcr.io/bootcrew/debian-bootc` carries `apparmor_parser` and 105 profiles
// and so declares it on its own row; `docker.io/library/debian:*` has no
// parser and an empty `/etc/apparmor.d`, so on that base it is this module's.
//
// `apparmor-utils` is here for `aa-status` alone: it is how a booted image is
// asked what it is actually enforcing, and neither deb base has it.
//
// No module preset: Debian's own postinst enables `apparmor.service` — checked,
// `apparmor.service.dsh-also` is present — so a preset naming it would only
// restate what the package already did.
packages "apparmor" "apparmor-utils"
